fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: ledgerlice
name: Ledgerlice
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Mook, attack +0, rating 3.
  level: 1
  role: mook
  armor: 0
  morale: 12
  weapon: A jaw built for one job
  wants: The nearest page, and then the next one.
  special: 'SWARM — a hit scatters the swarm instead of killing it: it is out of the exchange
    and back in the room within the hour. On a hard hit it also eats one written thing the
    target is carrying.'
  when_bloodied: null
  tells: Clean holes in the paper, exactly the shape of a paragraph, in a book that looked
    fine until somebody opened it.
  breaks: Cannot be routed. It leaves when the paper does, and a page laid down away from
    the party draws the whole swarm to it within one exchange.
  twists:
  - The swarm is four pages from eating the one paragraph the party came for.
  - It has already eaten the building's register, and nobody here knows what used to be in
    it.
  - It is in somebody's pack, and has been since the last library.
  - Someone has been feeding it on purpose, to make a record disappear.
  - The room is cold and the swarm is sluggish; warm it up and the swarm wakes.
  - An archivist is shielding the shelves with their own body and needs help, not rescuing.
  nastier: 'Wet ink draws it at a run: anyone who writes, reads aloud from a page, or works
    magic from notes in its presence is its only target.'
  description: >-
    Grey, flat, and the size of a thumbnail, with a jaw built for one job. A ledgerlouse eats
    paper, prefers ink, and will take a page out of a bound volume so cleanly that the book
    does not sag. An infested archive looks perfectly well until somebody opens something.
  notes: >-
    Level 1 Mook: no overrides. Fearless (morale 12) because it cannot be routed; its way
    out is the decoy.


    This is a problem, not a fight. A swarm is never fewer than a hundred, and counts as one
    to three Mooks by mass. It goes for satchels, scroll cases and open books before it goes
    for skin; characters are attacked only for carrying something written.


    Appears: never fewer than a hundred; counted as one to three Mooks by mass.
  reskin_of: null
